Sid Lee is a member of kyu, a collective of top-tier global creative companies established by Hakuhodo DY Holdings. Sid Lee also imagined C2 Montréal, one of the largest creative-business conferences in the world.

ROLE

The Senior Digital Project Manager plays a key role in the success of Sid Lee Digital. Responsible for large-scale projects and accounts, they ensure work is delivered on time, on budget and within profitability targets. With solid agency experience, they understand every discipline involved and act as a trusted partner to clients and teams. They also help evolve our practice and support less experienced project managers.

RESPONSIBILITIES

Lead multiple complex projects or accounts at once, from estimate through post-launch;
Own project financials: budget, profitability, forecasting and billing;
Manage scope: write estimates and statements of work, negotiate and document change requests;
Build the project plan and keep it in sync with the team daily;
Anticipate risks, put mitigation plans in place and escalate when needed;
Act as the main client contact, manage expectations and build relationships with decision-makers;
Lead key meetings (kickoffs, workshops, reviews, retrospectives) and report progress to stakeholders;
Contribute to qualifying business opportunities and to RFP responses;
Coach and mentor intermediate and junior project managers;
Help continuously improve our processes and tools, including through AI integration.

REQUIREMENTS

8+ years of experience in digital project management, a significant part of it in an agency;
Proven experience with large budgets and multidisciplinary teams;
Experience with website redesigns, CMS/DXP platforms or digital products;
Strong command of Agile and hybrid approaches, and of writing user stories and acceptance criteria;
Strong business acumen: profitability tracking, negotiation, scope management;
Excellent communication and leadership skills, including in delicate client situations;
Proficiency in French, both spoken and written, is required. Proficiency in English, both spoken and written, is also required to work with national and international clients and colleagues (50% of the time);
Proficiency with project management tools (ClickUp, Jira or equivalent);
Hands-on use of artificial intelligence in day-to-day work.
Understanding of traditional media and ability to manage non-digital projects (asset);
PMP, PSM/CSM or equivalent certification (asset)

Fier de souscrire au principe de l’égalité d’accès à l’emploi, Sid Lee s’engage à créer un milieu de travail reflétant la diversité. Toutes les candidatures qualifiées sont prises en considération, sans égard à leur citoyenneté, ethnicité, race, couleur, religion, genre, identité ou expression de genre, orientation sexuelle, handicap, âge ou statut de vétéran.

Nous encourageons les femmes, les personnes autochtones, les personnes en situation de handicap et les membres de minorités visibles et ethniques à postuler à nos emplois. De plus, des mesures d’accommodement peuvent être mises en place pour les personnes en situation de handicap qui en font la demande à tout moment durant le processus de présélection et de sélection.

Proud to be an equal opportunity employer, Sid Lee is committed to creating a diverse work environment. All qualified applicants are considered without regard to citizenship, ethnicity, race, colour, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, disability, age or veteran status.

We encourage women, Indigenous peoples, persons with disabilities, and members of visible and ethnic minorities to apply for our job opportunities. Additionally, accommodation measures can be made available for persons with disabilities upon request at any stage of the pre-selection and selection process.

